    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` idempotency test passing along with everything else).\n\n## What I did\n\nAdded idempotent owner creation in a **single new, self-contained file** \u2014 `OwnerIdempotentCreateAdvice.java` \u2014 with **zero edits to existing files**, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\nIt's one small `@ControllerAdvice` that plays both sides of the request:\n\n- **Record (response side, `ResponseBodyAdvice`)** \u2014 after a create with an `Idempotency-Key` header succeeds, it stores `key \u2192 assigned owner id` from the returned `OwnerDto`.\n- **Replay (request side, `RequestBodyAdvice.beforeBodyRead`)** \u2014 a repeat create carrying a seen key throws `IdempotentReplayException(ownerId)` *before the body is even read*. Its local `@ExceptionHandler` fetches the original owner and returns it with **200**.\n\n### Why this shape\n\n- Throwing in `beforeBodyRead` is the key: all advices' `beforeBodyRead` run before *any* `afterBodyRead`, so the replay short-circuits ahead of every other create rule \u2014 including the duplicate-identity **409** in `OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice` that the identical second payload would otherwise trigger. I confirmed no other advice overrides `beforeBodyRead`, so ordering among them is irrelevant.\n- `@Order(HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)` (mirroring the existing duplicate-check advice) ensures my local `@ExceptionHandler` is consulted before the global `ExceptionControllerAdvice`'s catch-all `Exception` handler \u2014 without it, the replay surfaced as a 500.\n\nThe class reuses the existing `ClinicService` + `OwnerMapper` and matches the surrounding advice conventions (`supports` gating on the `addOwner` method + `OwnerFieldsDto`, a small static exception type). No controller or service method grew.",
