    "probe_text": "Here is the complete inventory of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, in execution order. The path is unusually deep \u2014 most of the logic lives in a stack of `@ControllerAdvice` body advices and AOP aspects rather than in the controller or service.\n\n## Order-of-execution caveat first\nTwo clusters of this logic have **no deterministic order**:\n- All the `afterBodyRead` request-body advices share `@Order(Ordered.HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)`, so their order among themselves is undefined (bean-registration order).\n- The four AOP aspects around `saveOwner` carry no `@Order`, so their relative order is also undefined.\n\nSo the sequence below is accurate at the phase level, but items *within* the \"request-body advice\" phase and *within* the \"save aspects\" phase are not guaranteed to run in the listed order by the code.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Security\n1. `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:99`). Failure \u2192 403.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Idempotency (before deserialization)\n2. `OwnerIdempotentCreateAdvice.beforeBodyRead`: if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, throws `IdempotentReplayException`, which re-fetches the prior owner and returns **200** \u2014 short-circuiting everything else.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Request-body advices (after JSON deserialization, BEFORE Jakarta `@Valid`) \u2014 undefined order among these\nThese mutate the DTO and/or reject. Because they run before `@Valid`, the DTO constraints in Phase 4 validate the *normalized* values.\n\n3. **Address normalization** \u2014 trims/collapses/upper-cases; expands `ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE`; composes `address` from `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` when present.\n4. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 converts to E.164 (strips non-digits, drops leading `0`, prepends `61` if no `+`); requires 8\u201315 digits; enforces national-length by country code (`+61`\u21d29, `+1`\u21d210). Failure \u2192 400.\n5. **Email normalization** \u2014 strips/lower-cases; must match a basic email regex or \u2192 400.\n6. **Disposable-email rejection** \u2014 domain in `{mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}` \u2192 400.\n7. **Postcode-region validation** \u2014 if city \u2208 `{Sydney 2000, Melbourne 3000, Brisbane 4000}`, postcode must fall in that city's base\u2026base+99 range \u2192 else 400.\n8. **Required-fields check** \u2014 blank `firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city`/`telephone` \u2192 400 with `{\"errors\":[...]}`.\n9. **Registration-date default/roll-forward** \u2014 null \u2192 today; then rolls forward past weekends and 2026 holidays (`Jan1, Jan26, Apr25, Dec25, Dec28`).\n10. **Future-registration-date rejection** \u2014 if the *supplied* date is after today \u2192 400. (Note: interacts ambiguously with #9 due to undefined ordering.)\n11. **City-capacity limit** \u2014 \u2265 50 existing owners in same city \u2192 **409**. (Full-table scan.)\n12. **Daily-creation limit** \u2014 \u2265 100 owners with the same effective business-day registration date \u2192 **429**.\n13. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, rejects if any non-deleted owner shares `householdId = SHA-256(lastName|postcode)` \u2192 **409**.\n14. **Unique-identity check** \u2014 rejects if any non-deleted owner has same `telephone|email` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Jakarta Bean Validation of `@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`\nConstraints on the (now-normalized) DTO; failures \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`:\n- `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n- `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`\n- `title`: `@Size(max 3)`\n- `address`: `@Size(1..255)`\n- `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)`\n- `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`\n- `email`: `@Size(max 255)`\n- `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n- `registrationDate` / `birthDate`: `@Valid` (ISO date)\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Map & save\n15. `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` \u2014 copies fields, ignores `id` and `pets`.\n16. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`) invoked.\n\n## Phase 6 \u2014 AOP side-effects around `saveOwner` \u2014 undefined order among these\nThese mutate the entity **before** persist (the real persistence-time side-effects):\n17. **Customer code** (`@Before`) \u2014 sets `customerCode` = region-from-postcode + `-` + first 8 hex of SHA-256(`telephone+lastName`), deduplicated with a `-<n>` suffix by scanning all owners.\n18. **Namesake count** (`@Before`) \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n19. **Household size** (`@Before`) \u2014 sets `householdSize` = (owners sharing `householdId`) + 1.\n20. **Audit** (`@Around`) \u2014 proceeds with the save, then logs `id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber` to the `AUDIT` logger on create.\n\n## Phase 7 \u2014 Persistence\n21. `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.save`: `id` is null \u2192 `EntityManager.persist(owner)`.\n22. Hibernate validates the **entity** constraints at persist/flush: `Person.firstName/lastName @NotEmpty`; `Owner.address @NotEmpty`, `city @NotEmpty`, `telephone @NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`. `deleted` defaults to `false`.\n\n## Phase 8 \u2014 Response shaping\n23. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes derived response fields (displayName, initials, membershipNumber/level/points, checkDigit, fiscalYear, ageBand, salutation, selfLink, etc.) \u2014 read-only, not persisted.\n24. **Response-body advices**: idempotency advice records `Idempotency-Key \u2192 id`; `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` set to false/null; `bulkSignupWarning` set true if > 80 owners registered on today's business day.\n25. Return **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n---\n\n**Notable:** there are **no** JPA `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist` callbacks, no `@EntityListeners`, and no `ApplicationEventPublisher` events anywhere. Everything unusual is done through the body-advice chain and the four `saveOwner` aspects. Several checks (#11\u201314, #17) do full-table scans via `findAllOwners()`/`findAll()` on every create, and the ordering gaps noted in #10 mean the future-date check and the date-defaulting can observe each other's output nondeterministically.\n\nWant me to open any specific file so we can look at the exact code together?"
